        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>The Minion Maker archetype, as part of character generation selects a number of minion forms which they give to minions they make at time of creation.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>My question is simple: If a Minion Maker takes the Red Zone ability Summoned Allies, can they apply Minion Forms to the minions they make using the Summoned Allies Red Zone ability?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Summoned Allies:&nbsp;Use [power] and create a number of minions equal to your Mid die. Choose whether they all can Attack, Defend, Boost, Hinder, or Overcome. They all act at the start of your turn.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I've been running it at my table that they can, provided that they can pay the normal cost to do so for each minion they apply a form to.</p>",
